WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:08.960
THE BATTLE KEEPS HEATING UP! Because the One Piece&nbsp;
Manga just revealed that ANOTHER INSANELY powerful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:14.440
force is about to join the fight! In fact,&nbsp;
right at the end of the chapter we see some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:21.840
mysterious force destroy a marine battleship that&nbsp;
was sent to destroy the civilians who escaped from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:29.960
Egghead Island. And to make sense of what we are&nbsp;
seeing here, let’s first go back to chapter 1089,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:36.200
where we first learn that the ship with&nbsp;
all the Egghead citizens evacuated THE DAY&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:44.760
BEFORE. Which is a super important detail&nbsp;
we will discuss more in just a moment,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:52.200
but in that chapter we see that once the marines&nbsp;
had located this ship, Saint Saturn ordered their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:58.280
IMMEDIATE execution because he didn’t want&nbsp;
the Egghead secrets to escape the island.

00:00:58.280 --> 00:01:04.320
Now, if we jump back to the current chapter,&nbsp;
we know that SOMEONE destroyed that marine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:08.120
vessel that was sent to wipe out&nbsp;
the evacuating citizens. And the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.120 --> 00:01:14.720
reason this is so exciting is that if&nbsp;
someone is here taking out Marine ships&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:20.880
then that means that an entirely new group of&nbsp;
characters could soon be joining the MASSIVE&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:29.920
CHAOS going on at Egghead Island. But this&nbsp;
might not actually be who you would expect.

00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:37.240
Because the most straight forward assumption&nbsp;
that I think Oda wants you to make is that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.240 --> 00:01:43.280
this is the work of the Blackbeard pirates&nbsp;
since we have been waiting for them to do&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.280 --> 00:01:51.560
SOMETHING ever since we saw their ship arrive&nbsp;
at Egghead way back in chapter 1079. But this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.560 --> 00:01:56.920
ABSOLUTELY cannot be THOSE Blackbeard&nbsp;
pirates since we know the civilian ship&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.920 --> 00:02:02.600
left the day before the current events,&nbsp;
so they should be pretty far away at this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:09.520
point while those Blackbeard pirates were&nbsp;
on Egghead right before the battle started.

00:02:09.520 --> 00:02:17.200
So we simply must ask, if not those&nbsp;
Blackbeard pirates, then who could this be?

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:22.720
Well, the first option I’m going to throw&nbsp;
out, even though I don’t believe it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:29.320
would be the Straw Hat Grand Fleet. I mean&nbsp;
we’ve also been waiting for these guys to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.320 --> 00:02:35.200
do something for the longest time, but&nbsp;
we’ve seen Luffy in way worse situations&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:43.480
before and they’ve never shown up. So I’m not&nbsp;
counting on these guys showing up at this time.

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:53.000
The next option is that this could be A COMPLETELY&nbsp;
DIFFERENT group of Blackbeard pirates. Because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:59.040
remember that we know Blackbeard was somewhat&nbsp;
near Egghead since he clashed with Law soon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:06.280
after the Surgeon of Death left Wano, so it&nbsp;
is entirely possible that even if Blackbeard&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.280 --> 00:03:14.240
isn’t already at Egghead, he could be close&nbsp;
by on another ship. And if this is true then&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.240 --> 00:03:18.680
of course we just have to ask why he would&nbsp;
take out the marines, and the best answer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.680 --> 00:03:25.360
is not so he can save the citizens but so that&nbsp;
he could take them hostage and use them to get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.360 --> 00:03:31.120
something that he wants from Dr. Vegapunk.&nbsp;
Now, whether that is some sort of weapon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:38.720
or maybe some cloned devil fruits or something,&nbsp;
we can’t know. Or if he is making his way to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.720 --> 00:03:46.280
Egghead island, that would obviously add A TON&nbsp;
to the ongoing battle. However, even though I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.280 --> 00:03:55.000
think this is a strong option, it is far from&nbsp;
THE MOST EXCITING option that we have here.

00:03:55.000 --> 00:04:01.120
In fact, I’d be WAY MORE EXCITED if a&nbsp;
completely different Blackbeard pirate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.120 --> 00:04:07.480
was on their way because it is entirely&nbsp;
possible that the former Marine Admiral,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:14.640
Kuzan, could be the one traveling to Egghead.&nbsp;
And, WOW, if the Ice-fruit user truly is coming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.640 --> 00:04:20.240
to Egghead then there are SO MANY connections that&nbsp;
we have to make here. Because in case you forgot,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.240 --> 00:04:26.080
Kuzan was also present during the Buster Call&nbsp;
on the Island of Ohara, and that specific event&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.080 --> 00:04:33.800
has way too many connections to the events on&nbsp;
Egghead. Just start with the escaping civilian&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.800 --> 00:04:39.440
ship for example. Back on Ohara, the current fleet&nbsp;
Admiral Akainu destroyed a similar civilian ship&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.440 --> 00:04:46.560
to prevent secrets from escaping the island.&nbsp;
So wouldn’t it just be so fitting that Kuzan,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.560 --> 00:04:51.320
who was also present back on Ohara,&nbsp;
do the exact opposite of his marine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.320 --> 00:04:56.680
counterpart by saving the ship of civilians?&nbsp;
Because remember, at the Ohara incident,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.680 --> 00:05:03.560
Kuzan let another person escape - that of course&nbsp;
was Nico Robin - because he was unclear about what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.560 --> 00:05:11.040
was right and he hoped that Robin could prove&nbsp;
that to him with her actions in the future. So&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:16.440
by destroying this marine vessel here, Kuzan&nbsp;
could be showing us that he now has a clearer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.440 --> 00:05:22.960
sense of his own justice and is determined not to&nbsp;
let the marines kill any more innocent civilians.

00:05:22.960 --> 00:05:31.120
But that’s FAR from the only connection Kuzan has&nbsp;
on Egghead because if he is showing up, this would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.120 --> 00:05:39.920
also be the first time he sees Robin in over&nbsp;
two years. And I for one would be SO EXCITED to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.920 --> 00:05:48.000
see these two interact again, especially now that&nbsp;
the entire Straw Hat crew could actually put up a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:54.240
fight against the chilly former admiral. We could&nbsp;
maybe even learn just how much loyalty Kuzan has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.240 --> 00:06:00.240
to Blackbeard, as many people have even speculated&nbsp;
in the past that Kuzan has his own goals or even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.240 --> 00:06:06.520
that the former admiral could eventually join&nbsp;
the Straw Hat crew. Though admittedly that would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.520 --> 00:06:12.360
be a bit of a weird dynamic to have Robin and&nbsp;
the man who used to hunt her down on the crew.

00:06:15.560 --> 00:06:22.680
Besides that though, sign me up for a Kuzan and&nbsp;
Kizaru clash because I would just LOVE to see the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.680 --> 00:06:30.440
current admiral - who is basically a slave to the&nbsp;
world government - fight against the man who chose&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.440 --> 00:06:37.520
to leave the government. Who knows, maybe Kuzan’s&nbsp;
arrival could actually help knock some sense into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.520 --> 00:06:46.320
Kizaru, and convince the flashy admiral to protect&nbsp;
his friends instead of trying to wipe them out.

00:06:46.320 --> 00:06:51.480
On top of ALL THAT, Kuzan could also inform&nbsp;
the Straw Hats about Garp’s capture or death&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:51.480 --> 00:06:56.480
or whatever really happened to him, which&nbsp;
could actually pose an interesting dilemma&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:56.480 --> 00:07:02.440
for Luffy. If Garp is captured, does Luffy&nbsp;
abandon his grandpa and continue to Elbaf&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:02.440 --> 00:07:08.960
like we all assumed and was even confirmed by&nbsp;
Vegapunk? Or if he knows that Garp has been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.960 --> 00:07:14.640
captured by the Blackbeard pirates, would he&nbsp;
go off and try to rescue his Grandpa? Either&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.640 --> 00:07:20.000
way, we don’t know, but it would be super&nbsp;
interesting to see Luffy have to choose,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:25.320
and Kuzan could be the perfect one to&nbsp;
bring that information to Egghead Island.

00:07:25.320 --> 00:07:33.200
So yeah, clearly I’m all on board the Kuzan to&nbsp;
Egghead train, but that doesn’t mean there aren’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:33.200 --> 00:07:39.400
some other MIND BLOWING possibilities.&nbsp;
It could be Vivi and Big News Morgans,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:39.400 --> 00:07:43.760
who were supposed to be making their&nbsp;
way over to Egghead Island. And saving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:43.760 --> 00:07:48.880
a bunch of civilians is exactly the kind&nbsp;
of thing Vivi would want to do. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.880 --> 00:07:55.360
there’s even one more option that I actually&nbsp;
think could change the entire world.

00:07:55.360 --> 00:08:02.320
And honestly, the pace at which we’re going&nbsp;
here, 2024 is bound to be an absolutely INSANE&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.320 --> 00:08:06.960
Year for us. And if you have someone that&nbsp;
you can share your love for One PIece with,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:06.960 --> 00:08:13.080
that makes it just the more exciting if you can&nbsp;
just sit down and watch it together on the couch&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.080 --> 00:08:19.320
crunching down on some delicious snacks, though&nbsp;
it’s still pretty awesome even by yourself. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:19.320 --> 00:08:24.520
if you don’t know how to get THE perfect snack&nbsp;
to watch and read one piece to, don’t worry,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:24.520 --> 00:08:31.960
because I got you: This mysterious box is&nbsp;
from today’s sponsor Sakuraco, and it’s a&nbsp;&nbsp;

