00:09:52.240 --> 00:09:58.600
your first TokyoTreat order. Which actually&nbsp;
brings me right back to this chapter here.

00:09:58.600 --> 00:10:07.080
Because remember we still have THIS! Well, what&nbsp;
if this iron Giant wasn’t the only thing that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:07.080 --> 00:10:12.960
woke up after hearing Luffy’s heart beat. So yeah,&nbsp;
I’m saying there could be other ancient bits of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:12.960 --> 00:10:20.240
technology that heard the Drums of Liberation&nbsp;
and are heading to Egghead to find the source.

00:10:22.400 --> 00:10:27.640
Then of course there some other possibilities that&nbsp;
we just have to throw out there. The Revolutionary&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:27.640 --> 00:10:32.480
Army would certainly make a lot of sense for&nbsp;
why they would want to come. I mean, Kuma came&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:32.480 --> 00:10:37.760
to Egghead, and they were even discussing where&nbsp;
he could have gone so they probably want to save&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:37.760 --> 00:10:45.600
him if they can. This would also be THE PERFECT&nbsp;
opportunity to take down one of the Gorosei, which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:45.600 --> 00:10:53.120
is the main goal of the Revolutionaries in the&nbsp;
first place, but there is one MAJOR OBSTACLE for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:53.120 --> 00:10:58.720
the Revolutionaries to show up here. And that’s&nbsp;
because they are literally on the other side of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:58.720 --> 00:11:04.520
the world. Because as we know, the Revolutionaries&nbsp;
now have their base at Kamabakka Kingdom,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:04.520 --> 00:11:11.640
which is in the Paradise part of the Grand&nbsp;
Line while Egghead Island is literally on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:11.640 --> 00:11:18.840
other side of the world, near the end of the New&nbsp;
World. The only reason Kuma got here was because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:18.840 --> 00:11:24.760
he can fly super fast with his devil fruit, but&nbsp;
unless the rest of the Revolutionaries have some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:24.760 --> 00:11:32.800
sort of flying or transportation powers, I just&nbsp;
don’t see how they could arrive here so soon.

00:11:32.800 --> 00:11:40.000
However, an EVEN STRONGER&nbsp;
force is much, much closer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:40.000 --> 00:11:46.120
and that is of course the Red Hair Pirates.&nbsp;
Remember that we last last saw them on Elbaf,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:46.120 --> 00:11:53.360
which is relatively close to Egghead&nbsp;
island. And you might be asking, well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:53.360 --> 00:11:59.080
why would Shanks come to Egghead? And that’s&nbsp;
actually a great question because there isn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:59.080 --> 00:12:06.520
really a great answer. Of course, he could&nbsp;
finally want to see Luffy, or maybe he is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:06.520 --> 00:12:14.280
after Luffy’s copies of the Poneglyphs. But why&nbsp;
would he come at THIS SPECIFIC TIME? You got me…

00:12:14.280 --> 00:12:21.120
However, there is one person on Elbaf with direct&nbsp;
ties to many people at Egghead Island, and that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:21.120 --> 00:12:27.560
is the giant Saul, who we recently learned was&nbsp;
still alive AND protecting the knowledge that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:27.560 --> 00:12:33.640
was saved from the Library of Ohara. So if he&nbsp;
learned that Vegapunk was in trouble, then I’m&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:33.640 --> 00:12:38.840
sure he would want to help his former research&nbsp;
buddy. Plus there are Saul’s ties to Robin and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:38.840 --> 00:12:44.720
their eventual reunion which just has to happen,&nbsp;
but while we’re throwing out options then if Saul&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:44.720 --> 00:12:52.200
is coming to Egghead it would make sense that he&nbsp;
would be bringing a whole crew of giants with him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:52.200 --> 00:12:56.560
which would should be more than enough to help&nbsp;
the Straw Hats win the battle on Egghead Island.

00:12:58.960 --> 00:13:06.200
Let’s talk about that battle though because wow,&nbsp;
there was A TON to go over from this chapter. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:06.200 --> 00:13:12.560
marine battleships are going crazy bombing the&nbsp;
island. Saturn just ordered all the Pacificstas&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:12.560 --> 00:13:18.000
to fire their super lasers at Bonney and Kuma,&nbsp;
all while thinking how pathetic they are. Which,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:19.240 --> 00:13:23.840
part of me wonders if this is all going to&nbsp;
backfire on Saturn. I mean, we’ve spent this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:23.840 --> 00:13:29.120
whole arc going back and forth with whose&nbsp;
side the Pacifista are on. And in the end,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:29.120 --> 00:13:35.840
it seems like NO ONE can overrule Saturn,&nbsp;
but now there might actually be one person&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:35.840 --> 00:13:41.920
who can. That would of course be Kuma,&nbsp;
who was the original Pacifista that all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:41.920 --> 00:13:49.400
the others are based off of. So what if he&nbsp;
somehow gains control of them at the last&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:49.400 --> 00:13:55.000
minute. Maybe because of something Vegapunk&nbsp;
installed or through Kuma's sheer willpower,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:55.000 --> 00:14:06.840
and he orders them all to fire on Saturn instead.&nbsp;
THAT. WOULD. BE. INSANE! And I’m 100% here for it.

00:14:06.840 --> 00:14:11.800
Besides that though, we basically got an overview&nbsp;
of what all the other straw hats are doing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:11.800 --> 00:14:16.800
which is SUPER HELPFUL because there&nbsp;
is just SO MUCH to keep track of.

00:14:17.960 --> 00:14:22.920
First, and most importantly, we finally&nbsp;
got an answer to many mysteries from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:22.920 --> 00:14:27.800
last few chapters involving Luffy. We wanted&nbsp;
to know where he got his food and then where&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:27.800 --> 00:14:33.720
he disappeared to last chapter! And in a mind&nbsp;
blowing twist, it was actually revealed that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:33.720 --> 00:14:38.760
the World Government finally found a way to keep&nbsp;
Luffy from fighting them. They couldn’t capture&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:38.760 --> 00:14:42.880
him! They couldn’t defeat him with an admiral,&nbsp;
but in this chapter when Luffy was confronted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:42.880 --> 00:14:50.320
by the unstoppable temptation of this super high&nbsp;
tech food vending machine, Luffy was helpless.

00:14:50.320 --> 00:14:58.040
All jokes aside though, WHAT IS LUFFY DOING?!&nbsp;
I know he’s a hungry guy, and food is basically&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:58.680 --> 00:15:04.360
energy for him, but leaving a massive fight&nbsp;
while his friends are in serious danger just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:04.360 --> 00:15:11.200
so he can have another round of fast food&nbsp;
seems like just a step too far. Seriously,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:11.200 --> 00:15:17.420
Kizaru nearly took out Bonney and Kuma AGAIN!&nbsp;
Sanji is running back and forth like a mad&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:17.420 --> 00:15:26.000
man trying to save those two AND Vegapunk.&nbsp;
But nope, here’s Luffy just chowing down.

00:15:26.000 --> 00:15:30.160
Seriously though, I’m trying to not be too&nbsp;
disappointed with this and instead focus&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:30.160 --> 00:15:37.360
on why Oda would want Luffy to be separated for a&nbsp;
bit. And if you think about it, he does this quite&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:37.360 --> 00:15:43.240
often during major battles. We've often seen where&nbsp;
Luffy will be missing or trapped or something and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:43.240 --> 00:15:48.240
unable to help the rest of the crew. It happened&nbsp;
in Thriller Bark when he was getting his Nightmare&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:48.240 --> 00:15:53.840
power up and the rest of the crew had to hold&nbsp;
off Moria. It happened in Dressrosa when Luffy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:53.840 --> 00:15:59.280
ran out of haki. And even in Wano after being&nbsp;
smacked off the rooftop by Kaido. So it’s really&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:59.280 --> 00:16:06.560
not that unexpected, but usually, Luffy isn’t&nbsp;
CHOOSING to be separated like he is this time.

00:16:06.560 --> 00:16:14.720
But by doing this Oda lets some of the other&nbsp;
Straw Hats shine a bit. Like Sanji putting in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:14.720 --> 00:16:19.920
work in this chapter and Franky blasting Saint&nbsp;
Saturn in the previous one. Plus giving Luffy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:19.920 --> 00:16:26.400
a break allows us to rebuild some of our fear&nbsp;
of the main enemies since Kizaru and Saturn&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:26.400 --> 00:16:33.000
are truly threatening the rest of the group&nbsp;
while Luffy is taking his break. And I’m sure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:33.000 --> 00:16:39.360
will eventually pay off when Luffy or someone else&nbsp;
needs to step up and protect the crew once again.

00:16:39.360 --> 00:16:46.440
However, Sanji’s not the only one putting in work&nbsp;
though and after nearly twenty chapters of not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:46.440 --> 00:16:52.840
seeing half the crew, we finally got a recap of&nbsp;
what’s going on for many of them. Nami, Chopper,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:52.840 --> 00:16:59.640
and Robin are back in the lab. Brook is helping&nbsp;
the Lilith Vegapunk get the Sunny in position&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:59.640 --> 00:17:08.960
to leave the island. Zoro is still supposedly&nbsp;
fighting Lucci, which is honestly something I’m&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:08.960 --> 00:17:14.680
hoping we get to see more of. I mean, if not then&nbsp;
Zoro literally just had a major fight offscreened&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:14.680 --> 00:17:22.480
for twenty chapters. But I assume we’ll get to&nbsp;
see our green-haired swordsman soon since Jinbe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:22.480 --> 00:17:29.640
is heading off to either stop his fight or to find&nbsp;
him in case he is lost somewhere on the island.

00:17:32.120 --> 00:17:38.480
So in the end it looks like we are heading for&nbsp;
an escape rather than a full out fight like we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:38.480 --> 00:17:43.080
initially hoped for once Saint Saturn&nbsp;
arrived on the island. And truthfully,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:43.080 --> 00:17:48.400
I think an escape was always the most&nbsp;
likely scenario. No one even expected&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:48.400 --> 00:17:55.640
us to be at Egghead once we left Wano anyway, so&nbsp;
it makes sense we wouldn’t truly have a giant,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:55.640 --> 00:18:02.280
all out war. But if the crew does end up&nbsp;
just escaping, I will admit to being a bit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:02.280 --> 00:18:13.040
disappointed because of all the hype and promises&nbsp;
of a world-shaking event throughout the arc.

00:18:15.040 --> 00:18:19.720
I’m still hopeful for the end of this arc though!&nbsp;
And more than excited for whatever is coming next!&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:19.720 --> 00:18:25.200
And to bring this all back to the end of this&nbsp;
chapter, if this mysterious savior is in fact&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:25.200 --> 00:18:30.480
a group of giants coming from Elbaf to save the&nbsp;
